======================================================================================================================
SUMMARY
======================================================================================================================
  The Local Group's own v_f (195-226 km/s) is below v_cap, so MS3's local cap does not bind in its MOND zone (S1a: it acts only
  at z >~ 7, inside the point mass's phantom-free Newtonian zone) and moves R_0 by 0e+00 (S1b).
  What changes is the READING: the MOND-sector switch counts baryons + phantom (and the ambient baryons) instead of
  subtracting the full matter background, so the edge moves OUT by a factor 1.000-1.000 (S2), and R_0 rises:
  candidate cell, M_b = 1.145e11, no carrier: 1.334 / 1.398 Mpc (canonical / alt) against XR4's
  1.334 / 1.398 and the measured 0.96 -> +0.143 / +0.163 dex.
  The external field that would rescue it (~2e-03 a0) is ~17x what a KiDS-passing kernel lets through: the LG and
  KiDS pull the screening in opposite directions.

